   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to the designation of a portion of the state highway system to be known as the \"Charles Varese Memorial Highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "A9799",
    "basePrintNoStr": "A9799-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §343-x, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A9799\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the highway law, in relation to the designation of a portion of\nthe state highway system to be known as the \"Charles Varese Memorial\nHighway\"\n\nSUMMARY:\nThis bill would add a new section, 343-x, to the highway\nlaw. The section would designate the section of state route 25A in\nthe village of Northport, within the town of Huntington, county of\nSuffolk, shall be known as the \"Charles Varese Memorial Highway\". The\nbill also directs the commissioner of transportation to provide friar\nthe installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the state\nhighway, however the designation shall be one of a ceremonial nature\nand the official name of such highway shall not be changed as a result.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: On April 15 of 2005 Charles Varese was\nkilled on his\nway to the Northport Firehouse, where he bravely served his community\nas a volunteer firefighter. It is our duty to honor and memorialize\nthose individuals who exemplify the highest of admirable qualities in\nmen so that we may continue striving for greatness. Charles Varese's\nselfless acts in his service as a firefighter and community role\nmodel are a testament to his character. Men like Charles Varese are\nfew and far between, and as such must be acknowledged\n\nFISCAL IMPACT: Negligible\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
